  "title": "Virgil's Aeneid",
  "summary": "Between 29 and 19 BCE, the Roman poet Publius Vergilius Maro (Virgil) composed the Aeneid, a twelve-book Latin epic narrating the journey of the Trojan prince Aeneas from the ruins of Troy to Italy, where his descendants founded Rome. Commissioned and encouraged during the principate of Augustus, the unfinished masterpiece provided Rome with a grand national founding myth linking Augustan imperial rule to ancient heroic tradition, becoming one of the most influential works in Western world literature.",
